<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Central and Southern Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Stellaland</h1><p class="st-meta">1882 CE – 1885 CE · capital Vryburg</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Boer mini-republic around Vryburg, created by mercenaries paid in land, whose fate was decided by imperial rivalry.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1882 the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/batlhaping-chiefdom">Tlhaping</a> chief <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mankurwane">Mankurwane</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korana">Korana</a> chief <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david">David</a> Massouw fought over land west of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/south-african-republic">Transvaal</a>, both recruiting white <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mercenary">mercenaries</a>. Those who served Massouw received farms and proclaimed the Republic of Stellaland, named after a comet, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gerrit-jacobus-van-niekerk">Gerrit Jacobus van Niekerk</a> as administrator and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vryburg">Vryburg</a> as capital.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The republic had a Volksraad, issued postage stamps and joined with neighbouring <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/goshen">Goshen</a> in 1883 as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> of Stellaland. Its settlers farmed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a> and sought union with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/south-african-republic">South African Republic</a>, which would have cut <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain's</a> road north to the interior.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cecil-rhodes">Cecil Rhodes</a> and the Cape government pressed for British intervention. Sir <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-warren">Charles Warren's</a> expedition arrived in 1885, and Stellaland was absorbed into <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/british-bechuanaland">British Bechuanaland</a>; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vryburg">Vryburg</a> became its capital and later passed with it to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/cape-colony">Cape Colony</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/stellaland.jpg" alt="Stellaland" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Samhanin · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:First_flag_of_Stellaland.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1882 CE – 1885 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Vryburg</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Gerrit Jacobus van Niekerk</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Dutch Reformed Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Dutch</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/south-africa">South Africa</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Republic of Stellaland, United States of Stellaland</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1884&amp;focus=stellaland" aria-label="Stellaland on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5331 3167 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Stellaland lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5651 3423L5651 3423M5651 3423L5682 3386"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5651 3423h0M5682 3386h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5651 3423h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5651 3423h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Vryburg. <a href="/atlas?year=1884&amp;focus=stellaland">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
